{"title":"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The two congruent rectangles shown have\ndimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in. by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in. What is the area\nof the shaded overlap region?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/148875dde5914a90f580d82c6db9acf9e96db728.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] filldraw((0,0)--(13,0)--(25,5)--(12,5)--cycle,blue); pair A1=(0,0),B1=(25,0),C1=(25,5),D1=(0,5); draw(A1--B1--C1--D1--cycle,black); pair P,R; P=unit(A1-D1)+D1; R=unit(C1-D1)+D1; draw(P--(P+R-D1)--R,black); pair A2=(0,0),B2=(25/13,-60/13),C2=(25,5),D2=(25-25/13,5+60/13); draw(A2--B2--C2--D2--cycle,black); P=unit(A2-D2)+D2; R=unit(C2-D2)+D2; draw(P--(P+R-D2)--R,black); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"145\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that all the 4 triangles are congruent. This means the blue region is a rhombus.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> denote one of the sides of the rhombus. We then can create from this, by the Pythagorean Theorem:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf38e9838d8c9ec8266cd13a3e9084814beca7f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5^2+(25-a)^2=a^2\\]\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c2918067b98bdd33499f43225aac479ebcf1362b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[25+625-50a+a^2=a^2\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb9e955795d08f861e6316b531c06ddb1a15577.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[650=50a\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174939ec8a0aed568dd8f27260446a903f452599.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=13\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />\nThis is because the legs of the triangles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b7c4af551b09bc7481f8c360df3704f6b6a4e76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, from the given information, and the hypotenuse is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\nWe can now derive the legs of the triangle, which are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Using this to find the area of the unshaded triangles in the \"straight\" rectangle, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73aa375cbe35f1940c18eba546b33ee31f7449a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{5 \\cdot 12}{2} \\cdot 2\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />\nThis means the unshaded triangles have an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and since the rectangle's area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f95d5645fad28d611d78b6f3a18255d258237ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 25 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />;\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/6/0e6f6b8afa50cf5a35f423a63e5e0b9f62756f23.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[125-60=\\boxed{65}\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II\">2011 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2011 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_Northern_Colorado_Math_Contest\" title=\"University of Northern Colorado Math Contest\"> All UNCO Math Contest Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017162204\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 143/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1407/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 94/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3253/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.079      1 Template:UNCO_Math_Contest_box\n100.00%    7.079      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13580:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017162204 and revision id 284454. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}